# A destructuring `for [:x :y] in <expr>` binder lives only within its own loop body: reads of
# `:x`/`:y` inside the body (lines 6-7) resolve cleanly, but a read of `:x` after `end for`
# (line 9) has no visible declaration in scope (spec/grammar.md:128,137-138;
# spec/execution-model.md:1235).
for [:x :y] in [[1 2] [3 4]]
  print :x
  print :y
end for
print :x
